        "description": "Writes key.pub beside the key file and prints it with the gh command that uploads it as a signing key. Appends the key for user.email to the allowed signers file. Then sets gpg.format=ssh, gpg.ssh.program, gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile when unset, user.signingkey=<path to key.pub> and commit.gpgsign=true, and prints each changed value. A path, not a key:: literal, keeps git from passing -U. When git cannot write the global configuration, it prints the settings as a configuration block. It does not set tag.gpgsign.",
